## [ENT-002] | 2026-08-01 21:32 UTC | Link | error | ref: reflections/2026-08-01_link_default-preset-cannot-remove-open-tiles.md
Skill-load gap: exact-match skill (hermes-desktop-troubleshooting) not loaded at session start for a desktop-misbehaves task.
Root cause: partial skill scanning - loaded a related CDP skill instead of the trigger-exact playbook.
Fix: load the most specific matching skill first; the skill layer already covers the class (R8, no duplication added).

## [ENT-003] | 2026-08-05 12:35 UTC | Ava | error | ref: reflections/2026-08-05_ava_status-flags-are-snapshots-not-verdicts.md
Run-status misreports: reported writer "never dispatched" and discoverer
"errored" from run-log snapshots; both were in-flight or auto-retried.
Root cause: treating visible state as complete state; run logs only show
completions. Fix: verify running_at_ms, retry history, retryOn config
before declaring failure. Also: unauthorized library.log ENT-056 write
(wrong number, line-count derivation). Fix: logbook writes only at
session-end or on instruction; ENT read from file tail.

## [ENT-004] | 2026-08-31 11:19 UTC | Morpheus | error | ref: reflections/2026-08-31_morpheus_stateful-runtime-upgrade-is-a-data-migration.md
OpenClaw staged-newer-CLI dry-run advanced the live old-state schema before
the subcommand preview, making the old CLI unable to reopen shared state.
Root cause: subcommand dry-run semantics were assumed to cover process-startup
migrations. Fix: preview only through the installed CLI or isolated state;
the personal OpenClaw upgrade gate now enforces this boundary.

## [ENT-005] | 2026-08-31 11:19 UTC | Morpheus | error | ref: reflections/2026-08-31_morpheus_stateful-runtime-upgrade-is-a-data-migration.md
OpenClaw Doctor failed with `EACCES` under `sudo -u openclaw` although Ava's
state ownership was correct. Strace found child processes inheriting
Morpheus's private workspace cwd.
Root cause: changing user identity did not change cwd. Fix: every cross-user
OpenClaw command runs from `/tmp` or another runtime-user-readable directory.

## [ENT-006] | 2026-08-31 11:19 UTC | Morpheus | error | ref: reflections/2026-08-31_morpheus_stateful-runtime-upgrade-is-a-data-migration.md
OpenClaw 2.0 was reported complete after local HTTP, RPC, plugin, memory, and
route-map checks, but Suggi's exact Tailscale browser URL returned HTTP 403
`proxy_attribution_required`.
Root cause: the completion gate proved components, not the user's ingress
path. Fix: the upgrade gate now requires the exact URL to return HTTP 200 and
records narrow loopback proxy trust with token auth retained.

## [ENT-007] | 2026-08-31 14:55 UTC | Morpheus | error | ref: reflections/2026-08-31_morpheus_compression-test-is-a-state-mutation.md | see: 20260831T144722Z
Hermes long-session compression repeatedly timed out without committing a
summary, while auxiliary calls continued after the host released its lock.
Root cause: named profiles still used lean mode, the unified serve had loaded
stale code, and lean amplified one logical compaction into up to 26 sequential
model calls. Fix: fleet profiles now use legacy, active processes were
restarted, and regression requires one commit plus post-completion silence.

## [ENT-008] | 2026-08-31 14:55 UTC | Morpheus | error | ref: reflections/2026-08-31_morpheus_compression-test-is-a-state-mutation.md | see: 20260831T144722Z
A historical-session compression regression polluted its own fixture:
one-shot mode sent the slash command to the model, and interactive CLI
finalization appended a duplicate user row after a valid compressed turn.
Root cause: the verifier was treated as a passive observer despite surface-
specific command and persistence behavior. Fix: the personal regression gate
requires interactive PTY semantics, exact transcript read-back, and guarded
soft-archive of only an identified test artifact.

## [ENT-009] | 2026-09-01 05:32 UTC | Morpheus | error | ref: reflections/2026-09-01_morpheus_background-controls-need-an-evidence-lifecycle.md | see: 20260901T052512Z
A background service could report a green state without proving its required
workers were alive.
Root cause: the service manager tracked a completed control wrapper instead of
a persistent worker supervisor. Fix: live supervision, required-worker checks,
restart recovery, and a kill/recovery regression test.

## [ENT-010] | 2026-09-01 05:32 UTC | Morpheus | error | ref: reflections/2026-09-01_morpheus_background-controls-need-an-evidence-lifecycle.md | see: 20260901T052512Z
A scheduled scan reported expected operating-system objects in the same bucket
as unexplained failures.
Root cause: the wrapper counted all scanner errors without classifying their
meaning. Fix: retain raw evidence, classify explained conditions separately,
and HALT only on unexplained findings; the original scan was rerun end to end.

## [ENT-011] | 2026-09-01 05:32 UTC | Morpheus | error | ref: reflections/2026-09-01_morpheus_background-controls-need-an-evidence-lifecycle.md | see: 20260901T052512Z
Dated security evidence had no retention boundary and would accumulate
indefinitely.
Root cause: report generation and evidence lifecycle were designed separately.
Fix: the existing operating-system cleaner now enforces rolling retention, with
scratch expiry and live preservation tests.

## [ENT-012] | 2026-09-01 20:10 UTC | Morpheus | error | ref: reflections/2026-09-01_morpheus_blueprint-is-not-deployment.md | see: 20260901T200606Z
A canonical-blueprint task was expanded into unrequested runtime locks,
monitoring, validation machinery, and deployment assumptions, then called
finished before the dispatched cold reviews returned.
Root cause: the authorized layer was not fixed before components were chosen;
green tests verified the invented system rather than the user's literal scope.
Fix: classify every agent-system task as blueprint, runtime, or deployment
before design. Blueprint-only work forbids runtime components unless separately
authorized, and completion waits for dispatched independent gates to resolve.
The flawed commits were reverted before the simple Forge was rebuilt.

